Let jumps be a list of 2, 3, 1, 1, and 4.
Let farthest be 0.
Let possible be 1.
For every position from 0 to the last position of jumps.
If position is more than farthest, set possible to 0.
Let arrival be position plus item position of jumps.
If position is at most farthest, set farthest to the larger of farthest and arrival.

If possible is 1, print true, otherwise print false.
